WHAT: two more things in the WK_TFE_SELFTEST narration -- the Name field's
      rect (LENAME), and which widget currently holds focus (focus= on the
      STATE line).
WHY:  the harness can now TYPE into a real QLineEdit and prove the characters
      landed. Both additions exist because the obvious version of that test
      cannot tell its failures apart:
        * a QLineEdit only accepts text when it has focus, and focus is taken
          by clicking it -- which needs its rect, at a position only the
          laid-out app knows (same reason 0003 publishes BTNABOUT, and the
          same reason it is on the repeating timer: the wk QPA forces the
          first top-level to the full surface, so any rect read earlier is
          the pre-resize one);
        * without focus=, text that arrives while nothing is focused is
          indistinguishable from text that never arrived. One is a missed
          click, the other is a broken host input path, and the whole point
          of the test is to tell those two apart.
      name= was already read straight off leName->text(), so the assertion
      itself needed nothing new: it reads the string the user would see in
      the field, not a proxy for it.
UPSTREAM: no, same as 0003 -- ours, for testing, #ifdef __wasi__.
--- a/main.cpp
+++ b/main.cpp
@@ -349,14 +349,28 @@
                         ++tops;
                     }
                 }
-                std::printf("STATE title='%s' name='%s' hash='%s' size='%s' files=%d tops=%d\n",
+                // focus= is what makes the typing check honest. Text that
+                // arrives while nothing is focused goes nowhere and looks
+                // exactly like text that never arrived, so a harness that
+                // only watched name= could not tell "the key event was
+                // dropped" from "I clicked the wrong pixel".
+                QWidget *fw = QApplication::focusWidget();
+                std::printf("STATE title='%s' name='%s' hash='%s' size='%s' files=%d tops=%d focus='%s'\n",
                             qPrintable(w.windowTitle()), qPrintable(text("leName")),
                             qPrintable(text("leHash")), qPrintable(text("leTorrentTotalSize")),
-                            files, tops);
+                            files, tops, fw ? qPrintable(fw->objectName()) : "");
                 if (QWidget *b = w.findChild<QWidget *>(QStringLiteral("btnAbout"))) {
                     const QRect r(b->mapToGlobal(QPoint(0, 0)), b->size());
                     std::printf("BTNABOUT %d %d %d %d\n", r.x(), r.y(), r.width(), r.height());
                 }
+                // The Name field's rect, for the same reason BTNABOUT is
